{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 10.156,
   "text": "In my little town, the tornado siren only sounds for tests. First Wednesday of the month... at noon."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 10.756,
   "end": 14.169,
   "text": "But my grandpa gave me one rule about it."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 14.769,
   "end": 19.74,
   "text": "If that siren ever goes off on a clear night... don't go down to the basement."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 20.34,
   "end": 23.241,
   "text": "Stay upstairs. Lights off. And wait."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 24.341,
   "end": 29.845,
   "text": "Last night, the sky was perfectly clear. Stars everywhere. Not a breath of wind."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 30.445,
   "end": 33.965,
   "text": "At two in the morning... the siren started to wail."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 36.565,
   "end": 44.416,
   "text": "Porch lights snapped on all down the street. My neighbors ran for their cellars in their pajamas, dragging their kids by the hand."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 45.016,
   "end": 49.069,
   "text": "I stayed upstairs, in the dark. Just like Grandpa said."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 49.869,
   "end": 52.813,
   "text": "Ten minutes later, the siren stopped."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 55.013,
   "end": 60.496,
   "text": "Then a calm voice came over the speaker on the pole. All clear. You can come out now."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 61.396,
   "end": 66.388,
   "text": "One by one, the cellar doors swung open... and my neighbors climbed out."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 66.988,
   "end": 71.297,
   "text": "Slow. Stiff. Not talking. Not one of them went back inside."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 72.097,
   "end": 76.343,
   "text": "They just turned, all together... and looked up at my dark window."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 77.743,
   "end": 81.775,
   "text": "They're still standing out there... waiting for me to come down."
  }
 ],
